                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    jcr:title="Why we focus on preserving personhood"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/title/v2/title"
                                    type="h3"
                                    variant="h"/>
                                <text2
                                    cq:styleIds="[1659545825678,1659545835858]"
                                    jcr:lastModified="{Date}2025-06-06T03:00:09.199-04:00"
                                    jcr:lastModifiedBy="singarx"
                                    jcr:primaryType="nt:unstructured"
                                    sling:resourceType="abbvie-com2/components/text/v2/text"
                                    text="&lt;p>In the field of neuroscience, with many tough-to-treat disorders and a high unmet need, our scientists are relentless in their pursuit of raising the standards of care. But the brain is complex, and new challenges require new ways of thinking across all stages of drug discovery and development.&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;&lt;br>&#xd;&#xa;Our work is personal and our pursuit of delivering transformational therapies to help people preserve their personhood is unwavering. That’s why we are continuously exploring innovative, disease-modifying approaches to address some of the most prevalent and serious disorders, from Parkinson’s disease and Alzheimer’s to migraine, schizophrenia and stroke.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p>&#xd;&#xa;"
                                    textIsRich="true"/>
                            </container4>
                            <separator
                                cq:styleIds="[1662756486159]"
